{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Sunken Temple: a tank can taunt the Hakkar event summons off the starter (#12653)",
  "contract": [
    "#12653: once the Avatar of Hakkar event started, the creatures it summons stayed on the player who lit the",
    "altar for the whole event and a tank could not taunt them off. #11443 made them attack that player instead",
    "of the closest one, but it also fixated them, which ignores threat. The PR author ruled that they should",
    "only aggro the starter on spawn and then follow normal threat. Using the Hakkar Worship Altar 2310500",
    "summons the Shade of Hakkar 8440, whose SmartAI summons Hakkari Bloodkeepers 8438. A Warrior tank in",
    "Defensive Stance 71 stands beside the starter. A Bloodkeeper first aims its Shadow Bolt 12471 at the starter",
    "(the #11443 behaviour, asserted). Bloodkeepers cast from beyond Taunt's 30 yards, so the tank then steps up",
    "to the first Bloodkeeper's summon point (-434.5, 288.3) and taunts the nearest one with Taunt 355, and a",
    "Bloodkeeper must cast Shadow Bolt at the tank. A fixated Bloodkeeper never would. Health fixtures keep both",
    "players alive; both join world phase 1, where the altar and the event's creatures are."
  ],
